# vmci.fragment: applied after vmware.fragment when VMWARE=1 VMCI=1.
# The plain VMware profile has no channel to the host. This adds one: AF_VSOCK over VMware's VMCI
# (vmw_vsock_vmci_transport). The host is CID 2 as under Firecracker, so the guest side is unchanged:
# AF_VSOCK to CID 2 port 8080, or the AF_UNIX shim (socat UNIX-LISTEN:/run/egress.sock,fork VSOCK-CONNECT:2:8080).
# On the host, scripts/vmci-bridge.py accepts that and hands it to api-proxy.py's Unix socket.
# The guest still has no NIC and no TCP/IP: this is the only way out, and it reaches only the bridge.
#
# Cost: the VMCI driver (a PCI device the hypervisor presents) is guest-kernel code parsing host-supplied
# data, with its own CVE history. That is why vmware.fragment leaves it out; take it only for a guest that
# has to reach the proxy.

CONFIG_NET=y
CONFIG_VSOCKETS=y
CONFIG_VMWARE_VMCI=y
CONFIG_VMWARE_VMCI_VSOCKETS=y
